-- title:
--   Triviality of the Sigma-Algebra of an Almost-Surely Constant Map
-- statement:
--   This establishes triviality for a sigma-algebra generated by an almost-surely constant random variable.
--
--   Let $(\Omega,\mathcal F,P)$ be a probability space, let $\mathcal Y$ be a measurable space, let $f:\Omega\to\mathcal Y$, and let $y\in\mathcal Y$. Assume
--
--   $$f(\omega)=y\quad\text{for $P$-almost every }\omega.$$
--
--   Then the comap sigma-algebra `MeasurableSpace.comap f` is trivial under $P$: every set in it has measure $0$ or $1$.
--
--   This is useful for treating an almost-surely constant observable as a null-or-conull factor in subsequent independence statements.
-- source:
--   Lean source: https://github.com/cgarryZA/LevyStochCalc/blob/984dbf0b790031eac05d56fe5a84b65e15e1e932/LevyStochCalc/Probability/TrivialSigma.lean#L50-L67 (repository human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean, commit 408915f, module `LevyStochCalc.Probability.TrivialSigma`, declaration `LevyStochCalc.Probability.isTrivialSigma_comap_of_ae_const`; the repository is private at upload time). Vendored from https://github.com/cgarryZA/LevyStochCalc at commit 984dbf0b790031eac05d56fe5a84b65e15e1e932 (Apache-2.0; upstream copyright notice retained in the Lean text).

